hadiths[328]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2125","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) states that the payment of Sadaqah al-Fitr will be obligatory on every Muslim, big or small, on a “free slave” who will buy two half of wheat or one saa of wheat."
"2126","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that it will be two maunds of wheat or one saa of wheat."
"2127","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that your expenses will be calculated according to the calculation, it will be half a saa of wheat or one saa of dates."
"2128","Abu Qalaba says that he has told me that those who paid Sayyidna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA) paid half a sa' of wheat."
"2129","Abu Qalaba narrates that a person told me that he had paid one Saa of wheat to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA) on behalf of two men (i.e. half a Saa is required to be paid to one person)."
"2130","Hasan al-Basri narrates that when Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) was the governor of Basra, he said at the end of Ramadan, Pay Zakat (Zakat al-Fitr) for your fasts. The narrator narrates that the people started looking at each other and Sayyiduna Abdullah (RA) inquired who are the people here who belong to the people of Madinah? Those people stand up! And tell your companions about it, because these people do not know that this is the payment that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made obligatory on every male and female, free and slave, which is a saa of barley or a saa of dates or half a saa of wheat."
"2131","Hasan Basri narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, while giving a sermon to the people at the end of Ramadan, said, O people of Basra! Pay the zakat of your fasts (i.e. give charity at Fitr) the narrator says. People started looking at each other and Sayyiduna Abdullah (RA) said, \All the people who are here from Madinah should stand up and teach this to their companions"," because these people do not know that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered half a Saa of wheat or a Saa of barley or a Saa of dates for every free and slave\"" Mandatory on women. Hasan Basri narrates that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when Allah gives you prosperity"," you should pay one Sa'a of wheat."""
"2132","Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that before the people go to perform the Eid prayer, Sadaqah al-Fitr should be given (narrated by the narrator)."
"2133","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) made it obligatory to pay Zakat al-Fitr."
"2134","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has given this order: \A person should give Sadaqah al-Fitr before going to pray.\"""""
"2135","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has given this instruction about it: \It should be performed before the people go for the Eid prayer.\"""""
"2136","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that this is a Sunnah: \A person should not go to perform the Eid prayer until he has taken some food and given Sadaqah al-Fitr.\"""""
"2137","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that this is a Sunnah: \Ghusl Janabat should be performed with one Sa'a of water"," and ablution and one liter of water should be performed.\"" One Sa'a is eight Ritals. Regarding the narrator named Mansoor"," this hadith has been narrated only by the narrator named Salih and this person is weak."""
"2138","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to perform ablution with a bucket of water."
"2139","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with one mud (water) and one sa' (eight liters) of water."
"2140","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the husband of Sayyida Barira (RA) was a slave, his name was Mugheeth, that scene is also in my eyes, that man was crying behind this woman, his tears were flowing on his beard. Don't you wonder how much Mughees loves Breera and how much Breera dislikes Mughees. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to this woman that you should maintain your marriage with him, because he is the father of your children. This woman said, O Messenger of Allah! Are you ordering me? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \I am interceding.\"" The woman said"," \""There is no need for me to have intercourse with her.\"""""
"2141","Majlid narrates that I was the secretary of Jaz bin Muawiya, who is the uncle of Sayyidna Ahnaf bin Qays. We received a letter from Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, a year before his death. (The narrator says) We killed three sorcerers. We made every man to marry a wife whose marriage has been forbidden by Allah. Then they prepared a lot of food and invited the magicians. They placed their swords on their shoulders. The narrator narrates that Sayyiduna Umar did not receive jizya from the Magi until Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf testified that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) received jizya from the Magi who belonged to the Hijra."
"2142","Abu Muawiya narrates that I was the secretary of Sayyidna Jaz bin Muawiya, “We received a letter from Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (which contained this text) Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) told me that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, collected jizya from the Magi who belonged to the Hijra, so you should also collect jizya from the Magi of your region. The narrator of this hadith is not authentic."
"2143","A narrator named Bajla narrates that Sayyiduna Umar did not receive jizya from the Magi before, even Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) testified that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, received jizya from these magi. The narrator narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrated that once I was sitting at the door of the Prophet (PBUH) two men came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH). So both of them said (they have given this decision) Either we accept Islam or we are killed, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrated, then the people adopted the statement of Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman Bin Awf (RA) and abandoned my tradition."
"2144","Bajla Tamimi narrates that Sayyiduna Umar did not want to accept jizya from the Magi until Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf testified that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to collect jizya from the Magi who belonged to the \Hijr\""."""
"2145","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that if I had not seen my companions receiving jizya from the Magi, I would not have received it from them. Then he recited this verse (i.e., I would not have received it by the command of this verse) \And fight those who do not believe in Allah and the Last Day"," and do not consider that which is forbidden by Allah and His Messenger to be haram.\"" Act while they are disrespectful."""
"2146","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the people went out to see the moon. I told the Prophet (PBUH) that I had also seen the moon. So the Prophet (PBUH) himself fasted and ordered the people to fast too. Regarding quoting from Ibn Wahib, this tradition has been narrated by Marwan ibn Muhammad, who is unique and this narrator is reliable."
"2147","This tradition is also narrated along with an Usand."
"2148","Taus narrates: I was in Madinah, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas were also there. A man came to the governor there and testified that he had seen the moon (i.e., when he saw the moon of Ramadan). The Messenger of Allah accepted the testimony of one person about seeing the moon of Ramadan. These two men also stated that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, used to accept the testimony of only two men about the moon of Eid al-Fitr. The narrator named Abu Ismail Hafs is unique in narrating this tradition and it is weak."
"2149","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to observe the moon of Sha'ban, then he would observe the moon and observe the fast."
"2150","Saying salah, we were present with Sayyidna Ammar, may Allah be pleased with him, and a goat was roasted for him, and he asked to eat it: so a man withdrew."
"2151","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting for six days (the day of which there is doubt), the day of Eid al-Fitr, the day of Eid al-Adha, the days of Tashriq among the narrators of this hadith, other narrators are more authentic than Waqidi."
"2152","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates that there was a dispute among the people about the moon of Ramadan. Some said: It will be seen today. Some said: It will be seen tomorrow. So he answered yes! So the Prophet (PBUH) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal (RA) to proclaim among the people that they should fast. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast by looking at it (the moon) and end the fast by looking at it. If a cloud overshadows you, complete the count of thirty days, start fasting and do not fast the day before. Some narrators have also quoted this tradition as a Mursal tradition."
"2153","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: \A man came to the Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," and said: I have seen the moon.\"" He answered yes! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," “O Bilal! Announce among the people that they should fast tomorrow."""
"2154","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrated that a villager came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said: I have seen the moon. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “O Bilal! Announce among the people that they should fast tomorrow. The meaning of this hadith is close to the meaning (of the previous tradition)."
"2155","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2156","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a villager came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said, “I have seen the first moon.” The Prophet (PBUH) said, “Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad (PBUH) is the Messenger of Allah?” He said: Yes! So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced that people should fast."
"2157","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person came on a moonlit night of Ramadan and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I have seen the moon.' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah? He said yes! So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced that you people should fast. This tradition has been narrated by a narrator named Shuba as a transmitted tradition from Thori."
"2158","Ikrimah narrates that a villager testified before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he had seen the moon, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah? He said yes! So the Prophet (PBUH) ordered the people to celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr."
"2159","Ikrima narrates that the people had doubts about the moon of Ramadan. They decided that they would not fast the next day and not perform Taraweeh that night. A villager came to the service of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) from the rocky land. He testified that he had seen the moon. There is no god but I am the messenger of Allah? He said yes! But he testified that he had seen the moon, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal to tell the people to recite Taraweeh on that day (and fast the next day)."
"2160","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Before the moon of Ramadan is visible (do not fast as a precaution), however (if a person has a habit of fasting and it is a day, then he can fast) fast by looking at the moon and end the fast by looking at it. All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."
"2161","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this one or two days before Ramadan (do not start fasting as a precaution), then complete the count of thirty and finish fasting."
"2162","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission (stop fasting)."
"2163","This hadeeth was narrated along with another chain of transmission from Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) and all these chain of chains are authentic."
"2164","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When you see the first moon, start fasting, and when you see it, stop fasting, and if it is cloudy, then fast for thirty days."
"2165","Sayyiduna Rabi narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast it (on seeing the first moon) and perform Eid-ul-Fitr upon seeing it, and if it is cloudy, complete the thirty days of Sha’ban, then start fasting. (Look at the moon) This tradition has been narrated along with some other traditions."
"2166","Rabi' has narrated it from a Sahabi, the month (do not start fasting before it begins) until you see the first moon."
"2167","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Do not start fasting until you see the first moon, and do not end it until you see the first moon. If it is cloudy, fast for thirty days. This hadith has been narrated in Mota on the authority of Nafi on the authority of Ibn Dinar on the authority of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) in which there are these words: complete the count."
"2168","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this (the month) is sometimes twenty-nine days long. Narrated by Nafi) When the twenty-nine days of Sha'ban passed, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) would say to someone who was permitted to see the moon, 'If it was visible, then it would be fine.' The narrator narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar used to finish fasting with the people."
"2169","Rabi bin Harash narrates on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Beware! Before the month (of Ramadan) (do not fast as a precaution) until you see the moon (complete the number of thirty days) and do not fast until you see the moon (or complete the number). All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."
"2170","Rabi bin Harash narrates on the authority of one of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this. \Do not fast (as a precaution) before the month of Ramadan. Do not start fasting until you see the moon and complete the number of Leviathan. Then start fasting and do not stop fasting until you see (the moon of Shawwal) or complete the number of thirty.\"""""
"2171","This tradition is also narrated along with another document which is similar to it."
"2172","Abu Bakhtari narrates that we saw the Eid moon at the place of Zaat Shaquq. We doubted whether it was the first moon or the second or third date. So we sent a person to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Allah has related this order to seeing the moon. This hadith is authentic regarding its transmission from Shu'ba. Other narrators have narrated it on the authority of Amro bin Murrah."
"2173","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: (The narrator doubts that perhaps these are the words). The hadith is authentic regarding transmission from Shuba. Imam Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, has quoted this hadith from Shuba regarding Adam, and it contains these words: \You complete the number of thirty days of the month of Sha'ban.\"" In this hadith"," the word \""means\"" is not quoted."""
"2174","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Count the moon of the first of Sha’ban for Ramadan and do not combine Sha’ban with Ramadan."
"2175","Sayyidna Qays bin Talaq narrates from his father that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: \Allah has placed the first moon to count the days for people. When you see it"," start fasting"," and when you see it"," stop fasting"," and if there is a cloud over you"," complete the number of thirty. Muhammad bin Jabarrawi narrates that I heard this tradition from him. In addition"," I heard more narrations from Muhammad bin Jabernami narrators are not authentic"," they are weak."""
"2176","Sayyidna Rafi bin Khadij, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Take care of the number of Sha’ban for Ramadan.” Do not fast before the month of Ramadan begins. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned his thumb inwards."
"2177","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the month is sometimes twenty-nine days long, so do not start fasting until you see the moon, and do not fast until you see it, and if there are clouds, complete the number of thirty. Mina is the place of all sacrifices and Makkah is the place of all sacrifices. Hamad bin Zayd has narrated this tradition with reference to Ayub and has narrated it as a tradition that has been passed down to the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"2178","This tradition is transmitted along with another chain of transmission, however, it mentions that it was transmitted from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while there is also a continuation of the same tradition."
"2179","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH) \Start fasting by looking at the moon.\"" Then he has narrated the previous hadith according to it"," but he did not mention that \""the month is sometimes twenty-nine days long. The narrator of this hadith is Rooh Bin Qasim Al-Thaqa.\"""""
"2180","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that your fast will be on the same day when all the people will fast and your Eid will be on the same day when everyone will be celebrating the Eid."
"2181","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Fasting will be on the same day when you all fast, and Eid-ul-Fitr will be on the same day when you all celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr, and the Great Eid will be when you all offer Eid-ul-Fitr. The narrator of this tradition is weak."
"2182","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that when a person hears the call to prayer and has a vessel in his hand, he should not put it down until he fulfills his need. Imam Abu Dawud states that the authenticity of this hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Rooh bin Ubadah in the same way as described by Abdul A'la."
"2183","Abd al-Rahman bin Aish, who was a companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, says that Fajr is of two types, one that spreads in the sky in the direction of length, it does not interfere with a person's Suhoor prayer, it is not permissible to perform the Fajr prayer at this time, but when it spreads in the direction of width, then the food (of Suhoor) becomes Ihram at that time, and at that time you can perform the Fajr prayer. This tradition is authentic."
"2184","Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman narrates that I have come to know that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Fajr is of two types, one is like the tail of a wolf, it does not make anything halal or haraam, but the one that spreads in the direction of width, it becomes halal to pray and the (eating) of Suhoor becomes haraam."
"2185","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Fajr is of two types. One is that in which it is not permissible to pray (Fajr) prayer. Faryabi and other Muhadditheen have narrated it as a Muqoof tradition, while the students of Ibn Jaraj have narrated it as a Muqoof tradition with regard to him."
"2186","Salim bin Abu Ubaid narrates that I was under the tutelage of Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq, may Allah be pleased with him, one night he prayed for as long as Allah permitted. Salim narrates, I came out and came back and told him that the whiteness in the sky is moving upwards (in the direction of length). I came again and came and replied that the red has spread in the direction of the width in the sky, so he said yes! Now it's time, bring my breakfast."
"2187","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: \I said: The direction of the width is light and it is red"," so Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq (RA) said: Now bring me something to drink. Narrators narrate these words in a tradition. One day Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq (RA) said: \""Stand at the door (between me and Fajr) and tell me when (Fajr breaks) this tradition is authentic."""
"2188","Abdullah bin Nu'man narrates that once in the last part of the night in the month of Ramadan, Sayyidna Qais bin Talaq (RA) came to me. At that time, the Suhoor meal had been stopped due to the fear of dawn. He asked me for curry. I said: O uncle! If there is still some part of the night left, I will give you food and drink. Then they came inside, so I gave them meat and nabeez in front of them (Tharir). They ate and drank them and forced me too. So I also ate and drank and I was afraid of dawn. Then Sayyiduna Talaq has narrated this thing regarding the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. As long as the head does not spread in front of you in the direction of width, the narrator indicated this with his hand. His narrator, Qais bin Talaq, is not authentic."
"2189","Sayyiduna Samura bin Jund b, may Allah be pleased with him, said this while giving a sermon: \Do not let Bilal's call to prayer stop you from starting Suhoor"," and do not let the light that spreads across the horizon (in the direction of length) stop you as long as it spreads in the direction of width (you may eat Suhoor). This tradition is authentic."""
"2190","Sayyiduna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Do not misunderstand Bilal's call to prayer and this whiteness."
"2191","Hussain bin Harith narrates the polemical narration: The Governor of Makkah while giving a sermon to us gave this oath to the people and inquired who saw the moon on \so-and-so first\"" then he told us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed us (to sacrifice on the day of Eid al-Adha) if we do not see the moon ourselves and two righteous witnesses testify to this"," then we should offer the sacrifice (i.e. Eid al-Adha) on the testimony of both of them. Asked who the governor was"," he replied"," I don't know. After that"," I met him. He said that he was Sahib Harith bin Hatib"," who was the brother of Sayyidna Muhammad bin Hatib. His chain of transmission is connected and this hadith is authentic."""
"2192","Hussain bin Harith narrates, the governor of Makkah said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had instructed us to (sacrifice after seeing the moon), that is, to celebrate Eid-ul-Adha, and if we do not see the moon ourselves and two righteous people bear witness to it, then we should sacrifice on the basis of the testimony of both of them. So he replied that he was Harith bin Hatib, who was the brother of Muhammad bin Hatib. This governor also said that there is a person among you who has the most knowledge in the (rules) of Allah and His Messenger. Then this governor pointed to a person who was there. The narrator describes who he was? So he replied - He was Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA). Abu Bakr Nishapuri narrates that I inquired about this tradition from Ibrahim Harbi. He said that Saeed bin Sulaiman narrated this tradition to us. After that, Ibrahim narrated that he was Sahib Harith bin Hatib bin Harith bin Muammar bin Khabib bin Wahib bin Huzaifah bin Juma, who had the privilege of migrating to Abyssinia."
"2193","Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that we have the privilege of being in the company of the Companions of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. \Start fasting after seeing it (the first moon) and stop fasting when you see it"," and if it is cloudy"," complete the number of thirty. If two righteous people testify"," then start fasting (on the basis of their testimony). Perform Eid-ul-Fitr or sacrifice (i.e. celebrate Eid-ul-Adha)."""
"2194","Rabi narrates this with reference to a Sahabi: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting and it was the thirtieth day of Ramadhan. Dodihati came and they testified that there is no god but Allah and they said that they had seen the moon last night."
"2195","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrates that Sayyiduna Umar accepted the testimony of a person regarding the sighting of the moon on Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha. The narrator named Eid al-Ala has quoted Ibn Abi Laila in the same way, but the narrator named Abd al-Ala is weak. Similarly, the narrator named Ibn Abi Laila has not found the age of Sayyiduna Umar. Abu Wail Shaqiq bin Salama has narrated a different tradition from this. He has narrated this on the authority of Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, has said this: \You people should not fast until two men bear witness (that they have seen the moon).\"" This tradition has been narrated by Amish and Mansoor on his authority."""
"2196","Shaqiq bin Salamah narrates that we received a letter from Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. We were in Khanaqin at that time. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, \When you see the moon of the first day in the early part of the day"," then do not celebrate Eid until the third hour until two people testify that they saw the moon the previous night. This tradition is more authentic than the tradition of Ibn Abi Laila.\"""""
"2197","Abu Wail narrates that a letter came to us (at the place of Khanaqin) from Sayyiduna Umar (in which it was written): The first moon is sometimes small and large, so when you see the moon in the early part of the day, do not celebrate Eid until two men testify that they saw the moon the previous night."
"2198","Ibn Abi Laila narrates, \I was with Sayyidna Umar (RA) and a rider came to him and said that he had seen the first moon. So Sayyidna Umar (RA) instructed the people to celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr.\"" Muhammad bin Ali narrates: I asked Abu Na'im whether Ibn Abi Laila narrated the hadith from Sayyiduna Umar"," so he replied"," \""I don't know.\"" Muhammad bin Ali narrates"," I inquired from Yahya bin Mu'in whether Ibn Laila had heard the hadith from Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him)"," so he did not declare it to be correct. The tradition of Abu Wail is more authentic in terms of chain of transmission"," which is narrated by Amish and Mansoor with reference to Abu Wail."""
"2199","Abu Wail narrated that a letter from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us, and we were at the place of Khanaqin at that time (it contained this text) The first moon is sometimes small and big, so when you see the moon in the early part of the day, do not celebrate Eid until two righteous men testify that they saw the moon last night. Who is"
"2200","Abu Wail narrates that a letter came to us from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that we were in Khanaqin at that time (it contained this text) The first moon is sometimes small and large, so when you see the moon during the day, break your fast until evening, until two Muslims testify that they saw the moon last night (then you break your fast and celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr)."
"2201","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2202","Rabi bin Harash narrates on the authority of a Sahabi, there was a dispute between the people about the last day of Ramadan, 'the villagers came and they swore in the name of Allah in front of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and testified that they both had seen the moon last night. A narrator named Khalaf narrated this additionally: (The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed) People to come to the Eidgah (for the Eid prayer)."
"2203","Abu Umar bin Anas narrates this on the authority of his uncle. It was witnessed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the people had seen the moon, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the people (to break their fast and go for the Eid prayer the next morning). This tradition is good and the tradition after it is also good."
"2204","Abu Bashir narrates, I heard Abu Umayr bin Anas narrate on the authority of some of his uncles, Abu Nafar narrates on the authority of his Ansari uncles, they were present with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the latter part of the day, some riders came there and testified that they had seen the moon last night, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed the people that they should (break their fast and go to the Eidgah the next day) to perform the Eid prayer. go"
"2205","Fatima bint Hussain narrates that a person testified to Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) about seeing the moon of Ramadan, then Sayyidna Ali Bin Abu Talib (RA) fasted. The narrator narrates that he also ordered the people to fast and said, \I should fast on the day of Sha'baan"," this is better for me than that I should not fast on the day of Ramadan.\"" Imam Shafi'i says"," \""If the common people have not seen the moon of Ramadan and a righteous person sees it"," then I will accept his testimony because it is also transmitted by influence and caution is also in it"," but after that Imam Shafi'i issued this fatwa. The testimony of at least two people is a condition for Ramadan. Imam Shafi'i and some of our companions have stated this. This is Ruqiyas"," this is the order of witnessing about every missing thing."""
"2206","Imam Shafi'i says that whoever sees the moon of Ramadan alone, then he should fast on that day, and whoever sees the moon of Shawwal, he should not fast on that day and keep it a secret (but on the testimony of this banana, other people will not fast or not fast)."
"2207","Imam Malik states that whoever sees the moon of Ramadan alone, then he should fast because it is not right for him to fast now, because he knows that this day is part of Ramadan. Then he should state this when the moon appears in front of the people and they should say that we have seen the moon."
"2208","Abu Bakhtari narrates: We saw the moon of Dhu al-Hajj, and it seemed large to us. The person who described it as less, said it was the moon of the second night: And the one who was describing it more, he called it the moon of the third night. He said, \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has conditioned (the beginning of the month) with the sighting of the moon.\"" This tradition and the following tradition are authentic."""
"2209","Abu Bahtari narrates: We set out to perform Umrah. When we camped in Batin Nakhla, we saw the moon. Some said: This is the moon of the second night, and some said: This is the moon of the third. At night, he said, \This is the same night in which you saw it"," because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made his command conditional on seeing it. This hadith is authentic.\"""""
"2210","Abu Bakhtari narrates that we saw the moon of Ramadan. We were present in ``Urq. We sent a person to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) to inquire about it. He said: The Prophet (PBUH) said this. Verily, Allah spreads it out in front of you so that you can see it."
"2211","Kareeb narrates that Sayyida Umm al-Fazl bint Harith (RA) sent him to the service of Sayyidna Muawiya (RA) and he says, “I came to Syria to complete the work of Sayyid Umm Fazl.” At the same time, the moon of Ramadan was seen. I was in Syria. “I saw the moon on Friday night. When did you see the moon? So I replied, I saw it on Friday night. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) asked: Did you see it from God? I said: Yes! And the people had also seen it. I had also fasted. Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) had also fasted. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We saw it on Saturday night and we will fast continuously. He answered no! This is what the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has instructed us. This tradition is authentic."
"2212","Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the morning of the thirtieth day of Ramadan, Dudihati came and testified before the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he saw the moon last night. Chapter To make the intention (of fasting) at night."
"2213","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates this saying of the Prophet (PBUH). \The person who does not intend to fast before dawn is not fasting"," he does not fast.\"" Abdullah bin Ibadanami is unique in quoting this hadith from Mufadl"," but all his narrators are reliable."""
"2214","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this on the authority of Sayyida Hafsa (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “There is no fasting for a person who does not make it obligatory before he is righteous in the morning.”"
"2215","This is narrated along with another chain of transmission. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whoever does not make it necessary at night\"" this tradition is also chained together with other chain of chains."""
"2216","Sayyida Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \Whoever does not make it obligatory before dawn"," his fast is not fasted. Some narrators have narrated it as a valid tradition"," some have narrated it as the saying of Sayyidna Hafsa"," may Allah be pleased with them"," and some have narrated it as the saying of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar"," while some narrators have related it to Salem"," Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Narrated by Hafsah Radiyallahu Anhu."""
"2217","Sayyida Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that a person who does not intend to fast in the morning before becoming righteous, does not fast."
"2218","Saida Maimoona bint Saad (RA) narrates that I heard the Holy Prophet (SAW) saying, \Whoever intends to fast at night"," let him fast"," and whoever comes in the morning and does not intend to fast"," let him not fast.\"""""
"2219","Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Qais says that I heard the wife of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam), Mrs. Aisha Siddiqa (R.A.), saying that once on the thirtieth day, the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) woke up in the morning while fasting."
"2220","Salim narrates this about his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): Once he saw the Shawwal moon during the day, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: It is not lawful for you to break the fast until you see the first moon, when it is visible (ie at night)."
"2221","Mu'adhbin Muhammad narrates, I asked Zuhri about the moon of Shawwal when it is seen in the morning, and he said, I heard Saeed bin Musayyib say that if the moon of Shawwal rises in the morning until Asr (maybe these words are up to Maghrib), the moon of that night that follows will be counted. Imam Abu Abdullah says that everyone agrees on this."
"2222","Sayyida Umm Hani, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to her. A vessel was brought to him, so he drank from it. Then he extended the vessel to me. I said, I am fasting. Eat it."
"2223","The son of Sayyida Umm Hani (RA) narrates that he heard Sayyida Umm Hani (RA) saying, \A drink was brought to the Prophet (PBUH).\"" He drank it"," and then extended it to me. \""Then I said"," \""O Prophet of God! I was fasting","' then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," 'Did you fast? They did not submit! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," then there is no harm to you. The wording of this hadith has been disputed in narrating from a narrator named Sumak."""
"2224","Sayyida Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that a drink was brought before the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He drank it and gave it to me to drink, so I also drank it. I said, O Messenger of Allah! I was fasting, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “A person who observes post-post-fasting is (Amin) about his will (the narrator doubts that he may say these words) is amir (i.e. he owns his will) i.e. he can keep the fast if he wants to and break it if he wants to.” Shuba narrates, I inquired, have you heard this hadith from Sayyida Umm Hani? So he said: No! This hadith has been narrated by our family and Abu Salih, a narrator named Shuba narrates."
"2225","The same hadith is narrated from Sayyida Umm Hani (RA) along with another chain of transmission."
"2226","Sayyida Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank a drink and gave his remaining drink to Sayyida Umm Hani (may God be pleased with him), so Sayyida Umm Hani also drank it. There are such words in a tradition narrated by a narrator named Abu Awana. \The narrator's saying that this hadith is narrated from Yahya bin Ja'd is an illusion of a narrator named Waleed and this narrator is weak.\"""""
"2227","Harun narrates this from his grandmother (Sayyida Umm Hani, may Allah be pleased with him) I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I was fasting. If it was a fast of expiation, then you should fast one day instead of it, and if it was a fast of post-post-mortem, then if you want to make up for it, then if you want, do not make up for it. This hadith has been narrated by Hatim bin Abu Saghira on the authority of Samak on the authority of Abu Salih on the authority of Sayyidah Umm Hani."
"2228","Sayyida Umm Hani, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the one who fasts post-natally has the right to keep the fast if he wishes."
"2229","Sayyidah Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “A person who fasts after fasting is Amin (the narrator has doubts) about himself, Ameer (i.e. he is the owner of his own will) whether he keeps the fast or breaks it if he wants. Sumak has heard this hadith from the son of Sayyida Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with him) 'Allah knows the rest."
"2230","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) that he did not think there was any problem in breaking the post-natal fast."
"2231","Sayyidah Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes intend to fast in the morning. Sayyidah Umm Salma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said yes! But there is nothing wrong with me breaking the fast while it is Nazr Kana or Ramadan Kana. The narrator named Muhammad Bin Ubaidullah is Arzmi and this narrator is weak."
"2232","Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to like one food. I did not submit! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then I will fast.\"""""
"2233","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and asked, “Do you have anything (to eat)?” I did not submit! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then I fast.\"" Then one day"," the Prophet (peace be upon him) came to me and asked"," \""Do you have anything to eat?\"" I said yes! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""Then I will eat.\"""""
"2234","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when a person fasts after fasting, he can break it whenever he wants."
"2235","Aoun bin Abu Huhaifa narrates this with reference to his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made Sayyiduna Sulaiman Farsi and Sayyidna Abu Dardaa (may Allah be pleased with them) each other's mouths. He replied, \Your brother recites Bharnaful all night long. He fasts during the day. He has no need of the world and his wife. Then Sayyidna Abu Darda came. He welcomed Sayyidna Sulaiman. He gave food in front of him. Sayyiduna Sulaiman said to him: Eat too.\"" The Prophet (may Allah be pleased with him) also said: I will not eat until you eat. Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (may Allah be pleased with him) ate with him. Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) went to him at night. When it was night"," Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (may Allah be pleased with him) wanted them to start performing Nawafil. So Sayyiduna Salman stopped them and said to them: Your body has a right over you and your Lord has a right over you. You also have the right to observe the post-post-fasting and even leave it for a day. Abu Darda came to the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) to tell him about what Sayyiduna Salman (Radi Allahu Anhu) said to him: So the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said to him"," O Abu Darda! Your body also has a right over you. He said the same thing that Sayyidna Salman said. These words of tradition are from a narrator named Abu Talib."""
"2236","Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that sometimes the Holy Prophet (PBUH) would come to us and ask, \Do you have anything to eat?\"" If we answer yes! So you would eat it and if we ask"," yes! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: I fast. Once you came to us"," we were sent a gift (Hays). I said"," O Messenger of Allah! We have been given the gift of ``what I have kept for you.'' So he said"," ``I intended to fast in the morning","'' but then you ate it. This hadith is authentic."""
"2237","Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) came to me and said: I have intended to fast. Then Hays was brought to your service. In these words, this hadith has been quoted only by Bahli, 'no one else has copied it and no one has followed it', i.e. these words, \I will fast again in its place. Perhaps this matter has become suspicious for them"," 'Allah knows best'"," because other narrators have disagreed with Ibn Uyaynah in copying these words."""
"2238","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would ask for something to eat and if he did not get anything on that day, he would fast on that day. Abdullah, the narrator of this tradition, is not known."
"2239","Ibrahim bin Ubaid narrates that once Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) prepared food and invited the Prophet (PBUH) and some of his companions, one of the people present said: I have stopped fasting. The Prophet (PBUH) said: Your brother has prepared food for you. Your brother has arranged for you."
"2240","Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whoever forgetfully eats something in the month of Ramadan"," then it will not be necessary to make up for it. Allah will have fed and watered him.\"""""
"2241","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that one of the companions of the Prophet (PBUH) prepared food. He invited the Prophet (PBUH) and his companions. 'The food was brought.' Then one of those people retreated. 'The Prophet (PBUH) asked him what happened to you?' He said, \I have fasted.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him"," \""Your brother has arranged and prepared it for you"," and now you are saying"," \""I have fasted.\"" Eat it and instead of this fast"," fast another day.\"""""
"2242","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that if a fasting person forgets to eat something, then this is the sustenance that Allah has given him. Its chain of transmission is correct and all its narrators are trustworthy."
"2243","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that if someone forgetfully eats something in the month of Ramadan (while fasting), then no expiation will be required for him and no disbeliever will be required for him. A narrator named Muhammad bin Marzooq is unique in narrating this tradition and it is reliable that he is the one who narrated this tradition from Muhammad bin Abdullah Ansari."
"2244","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: If one of you eats something forgetfully or drinks something forgetfully (in the month of Ramadan), it will not be necessary to make up for it."
"2245","The same hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) with reference to another chain of transmission."
"2246","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Whoever eats or drinks something while forgetting (the duty of fasting)"," then he should maintain his fast"," and it will not be necessary to make up for it. The narrator of this hadith is Narrator Nazrbin Tarif"," Abu Juzi is weak.\"""""
"2247","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “Whoever forgets to eat or drink something in Ramadan (while fasting) then completes his fast, and it will not be necessary to make up for it. The narrator named Yasin is weak and the narrator named Abdullah bin Saeed is also like him (weak)."
"2248","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever forgets to eat or drink something (while fasting), then this is the sustenance that Allah has given him. Both the narrators of this tradition, Mandal and Abdullah bin Saeed, are weak."
"2249","Waleed bin Abdul Rahman narrates that he heard Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) mentioning that he had forgotten to eat something on the first day of Ramadan, he said, “I mentioned this to the Prophet (PBUH).” The Prophet (PBUH) said, “Complete your fast.” Indeed, ALLAH has fed and watered you, and there is no obligation on you."
"2250","This tradition is also narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, along with another chain of transmission."
"2251","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever forgets to eat or drink something, then he should not break the fast because this is the sustenance that Allah has given him."
"2252","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about a person who forgot to eat something and he is fasting."
"2253","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “After this, there is a hadith according to the previous one, its chain of transmission is authentic.”"
"2254","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (while fasting in the month of Ramadan). Abu Bakr Nahishli has narrated the same words following him and this narrator is reliable."
"2255","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss her during the month of Ramadan."
"2256","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss him while he was fasting in the month of Ramadan, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to have the most control over himself."
"2257","Dawood bin Abu Asim narrates that he heard Saeed bin Musaib narrating that once Sayyiduna (R.A.) came to his companions and inquired, \What are the people's opinions about what I have done today?\"" In the morning"," I had fasted"," then a maid passed by me"," I liked her"," so I had intercourse with her"," people felt this act of hers was very wrong"," while Sayyidna Ali remained silent"," Sayyidna Umar inquired"," what do you say? He said"," \""You have committed a halal deed"," and instead of this day"," you should fast on another day.\"" Then Sayyiduna Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said"," \""You have given the best fatwa of all of them.\"""""
"2258","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (RA) narrates that once the Prophet (PBUH) vomited, so he broke it. The narrator narrates that later I met Sayyidna Thawban, a freed slave of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) in the Jama Masjid of Damascus. The name of a narrator of this hadith according to one view is Ma'dan bin Abu Talha and according to another view it is Ma'dan bin Talha."
"2259","Sayyidna Fazala bin Ubaid narrates that once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting, he vomited, so he broke his fast."
"2260","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, \I used to not consider it abhorrent for a fasting person to touch his back.\"" Once Sayyidna Ja'far bin Abu Talib (may God be pleased with him) was fasting and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him. It is narrated that Sayyiduna Anas used to pray while fasting. All the narrators of this tradition are reliable and I do not know of any reason for it."""
"2261","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that it is permissible to make a fasting person sit on his back. The narrator of this hadith is Abdul Aziz."
"2262","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed the fasting person to make his back. All the narrators of this hadith are trustworthy."
"2263","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that kissing and kissing a fasting person is permitted."
"2264","Ayyub bin Muhammad Ajli, on the authority of the son of Sayyidna Anas bin Malik, narrates this on the authority of his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast on the 17th day of Ramadan, although he had previously said that the fast of one who fasts and fasts is broken. There has been a dispute regarding the transmission of this tradition from a narrator named Yasin and this narrator is weak."
"2265","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to fasten his legs while he was fasting."
"2266","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to fast on the 17th day of Ramadan, although he had previously said that the fast of both the one who drives and the one who drives is broken."
"2267","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to fasten his heels, although he had previously said that the fast of the one who puts on his heels and the one who is doing them is broken."
"2268","Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave permission for a fasting person to kiss and touch each other."
"2269","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that three things do not break the fast: vomiting, belching, and defecation."
"2270","Sayyiduna Maimuna bint Saad (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about a person who kisses his wife even though both of them have fasted."
"2271","This tradition is also narrated along with another document, however, this is not proven."
"2272","Sayyidna Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was fasting. This is not the fasting of Ramadan. He had a problem that was painful for him. Then he vomited. Then he asked for water for ablution. Is it obligatory to perform ablution after vomiting? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \If this was obligatory"," you would have mentioned it in the Qur'an.\"" The narrator narrates that after that"," the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted the next day"," so I heard him saying"," \""This is in return for my breaking the fast of the previous day.\"""""
"2273","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever vomits on purpose, Qadaa will be obligatory on him, and whoever vomits, Qadaa will not be obligatory on him. All the narrators of this hadith are trustworthy."
"2274","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2275","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates this saying of the Prophet (PBUH) \When a fasting person vomits with his mouth full"," it is not necessary for him to break his fast and then it is not necessary to make up for it.\"" If he intentionally vomits"," then it is necessary to make up for it."""
"2276","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Whoever vomits with his mouth full"," he must complete his fast"," and he will have to make up for it"," and whoever vomits on purpose"," he must make up for it.\"""""
"2277","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would break his fast, he would eat a few dates or a few chawhars, and if he did not have that, he would drink a few sips of water."
"2278","Thabit Banani narrates that he heard Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrating that the Prophet (PBUH) used to break his fast after eating a few dates."
"2279","Marwan narrates that I saw Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him, that he was holding his beard in his fist and was cutting off the part that was more than a fist."
"2280","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates what the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say at the time of breaking the fast: \O Allah! We have fasted for You and we have broken the fast from the sustenance that You have given us.\"" So accept it from us."""
"2281","Urwa quoted Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA), while Salim quoted it on Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA), both of them said that fasting on these days is only for the person who has a sacrificial animal."
"2282","This hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission and its chain of transmission is correct."
"2283","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says that the Prophet (PBUH) permitted a person performing Hajj to fast during the days of Tashreeq if he does not have an animal for sacrifice."
"2284","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the permission to fast during the days of Tashreeq is only for those performing Hajj who have a sacrificial animal with them. This hadith is authentic."
"2285","Urwa Bin Zubair has narrated this. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa and Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA) have both narrated this. The Prophet (PBUH) also did not allow a person to fast during the days of Tashreek, except for a person who performs Hajj (and has an animal with him) and a person who is besieged. This person is Abu Maryam Al-Kufi and he is weak."
"2286","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that whoever has a sacrificial animal with him should fast three days before the sacrifice, and whoever could not fast during those three days should fast during the days of Tashreeq (i.e. the days of menstruation). The narrator of this hadith is weak."
"2287","Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyidna Abdullah bin Hudhafa (may Allah be pleased with him) to go round Mina (to announce) that you should not fast during these days! Because these are the days of eating and drinking and the days of remembering Allah."
"2288","This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2289","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Hudhafa Sahmi (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) instructed a few people, including him, that on the occasion of Hajj Al-Wadaa, they should go around in the manna on the day of sacrifice and announce that these are the days of eating and drinking and remembering Allah."
"2290","Masoud bin Huqam narrates this on the authority of one of the Companions of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) that the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) instructed Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Hudhafa (R.A.) to announce during the days of Tashreeq, beware! These are the days of Eid and the days of eating, drinking and dhikr, so only the person who is performing Hajj and has a sacrificial animal with him should fast on those days, and the person who has not fasted continuously during the days of Hajj can fast on those days. The narrator of this hadith is Sulaiman bin Abu Dawood weak. This hadith has been quoted by Zubaid on the authority of Zuhri, which he has quoted on the authority of Masood bin Haqam on the authority of one of the Prophet’s Companions. The narrator of this hadith is Sulaiman bin Abu Dawud is weak. This hadith has been quoted by Zubaydi on the authority of Zuhari, which he has quoted on the authority of Masood bin Haqam, on the authority of a companion of the Prophet, peace be upon him."
"2291","Muhammad bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, \I attended the service of Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) in the month of Ramadan. He was about to set out on a journey. His horse was ready and he had put on his clothes for the journey. The sun was about to set. He ordered food and ate it. Then he mounted. I said to him: Is this Sunnah?\"" He said: Yes!"""
"2292","Narrated Amro bin Amir, may Allah be pleased with him: I heard Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, say: Sayyidna Abu Musa said to me: I have been told that when you leave (on a journey), you leave fasting, and when you enter a city, you are in a state of fasting. (i) entered into a state without fasting."
"2293","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Umrah in the month of Ramadan. The Prophet (peace be upon him) did not fast. I was fasting. My parents are sacrificed for you! You did not fast and I fasted. You offered a short prayer. I offered a full prayer. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Aisha! You have done well."
"2294","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Umrah, 'I was with him,' the Prophet (PBUH) offered a short prayer, 'I offered the full prayer,' 'He did not fast and I fasted,' when I reached Makkah, I said, O Messenger of Allah! My parents are sacrificed for you! You offered a short prayer, I offered a complete prayer, you did not fast, I fasted, then the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said, Aisha! You have done well. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not object to me in this regard. A narrator named Abd al-Rahman has found the time of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, when she was near puberty, she was with her father at that time."
"2295","Abd al-Rahman bin Aswad narrates that I went to the service of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her. She had a gentleman with her. She said, O mother! What makes Ghusl obligatory? Tawseedah Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that when the private parts are found, then Ghusl becomes obligatory."
"2296","Abd al-Rahman bin Aswad narrates that my father used to send me to the service of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her. I used to ask her when the year came in which I had a heart attack. Have you made this move? Then they pulled down the curtain between me and themselves."
"2297","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed all of these actions, he performed both full and short prayers, he fasted and did not fast during the journey, and the narrator of this hadith is weak."
"2298","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray both short and full prayers while traveling."
"2299","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in full while traveling, and sometimes he would offer short prayers. The narrator of this narration is not authentic."
"2300","Amro bin Shoaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: I have seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) both fasting and not fasting during the journey."
"2301","Sayyidna Hamza bin Umar Wasalmi (RA) narrates that he said, O Messenger of Allah! I find the strength to fast during the journey. Will there be any sin on me (if I fast)? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “This is a leave from Allah, whoever accepts it, he will do good.” And whoever wants to fast, there is no sin on him. The chain of transmission of this tradition is authentic. He narrated it from Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) with reference to her father. Sayyidna Hamza bin Amro asked that there is a possibility that both these traditions are correct. Allah knows best."
"2302","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) traveled in the month of Ramadan and he fasted. Once he traveled in the month of Ramadan, he did not fast."
"2303","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that a person attended the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I have become a victim of death, you discovered your potential! what happened He said, \I have intercourse with my wife during the day in Ramadan.\"" The narrator narrates that the Prophet"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," said"," \""Free a slave.\"" He said"," \""I do not have that.\"" Then a sack of dates came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which contained fifteen saa of dates. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""Give it as charity to the poor.\"" He asked"," \""Should I give charity to people poorer than my own house?\"" There is no one more needy than my family between the two sides of Madinah Munawarah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled until his wisdom teeth were visible. Seek forgiveness from Allah and feed this to your family. Its chain of transmission is authentic."""
"2304","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace. A sack was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there were 15 saa of dates. And feed sixty poor people on your behalf."
"2305","The same hadith is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) on the authority of the Prophet (PBUH), but it contains these words: A sack was brought to the service of the Prophet (PBUH), which contained fifteen sa’a of dates. In this tradition, the Prophet (PBUH) said, “Eat it and let your family eat it.” Fast for one day and seek forgiveness from Allah."
"2306","Mujahid narrated this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered the person who broke his fast during the day in the month of Ramadan to pay Zaharka Kaffarah."
"2307","Along with another hadith, this has been narrated from Mujahid as a messenger, and in one hadith regarding Mujahid, it has been narrated from Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) the narrator of this hadith is not authentic."
"2308","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that a person ate (i.e. broke his fast) in the month of Ramadan, and the Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to free a slave or to fast for two months or to feed sixty poor people."
"2309","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (PBUH), he (PBUH) said, “Whoever breaks his fast for one day in the month of Ramadan while he is present, then he should sacrifice an animal."
"2310","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever breaks one fast of Ramadan (or does not keep it) without an excuse, then he must fast for thirty days, and whoever breaks two fasts, he must fast sixty, and whoever breaks three fasts, he must fast ninety."
"2311","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Whoever does not fast for one day of Ramadan without any excuse"," he will be required to fast for a month. The narrator of this hadith is weak.\"""""
"2312","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may God be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that after half of Sha’ban has passed, one should not fast until Ramadan comes."
"2313","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) “Whoever is required to fast in Ramadan, he should continue it and keep the fast (and not leave it in between)."
"2314","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has given this advice about the Qadaa of Ramadan: \A person should continue it and do not make any difference in it.\"""""
"2315","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated that this verse was revealed, \so it will be counted in other consecutive days"," after which the word \""consecutive\"" was omitted."""
"2316","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates that this verse was revealed, \So it will be counted in other days which will be tarohogi\"" then after that the word \""Lagatar\"" was dropped."""
"2317","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about making up for Ramadan, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “He will make up the fast of this fast, if he makes a difference in the middle, it will be permissible for him to do so.”"
"2318","Abu Aamir Huzni narrates that I cursed Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with him, and he was asked about the Qada of Ramadan. He said, \Surely Allah has not given you this leave. You do not fast"," nor does He want you to suffer hardship in regard to its Qada.\"""""
"2319","Abu Amir Hozni narrates that I cursed Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah bin Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him about performing Ramadan separately, so he said, count the number and fast as you wish."
"2320","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) has narrated this about the Qadaa of Ramadan (he says): Take it as you wish."
"2321","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas and Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) have said that there is no problem in keeping the Qada of Ramadan differently."
"2322","Sayyidna Rafi Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) says that you should keep count and fast as you wish."
"2323","Abdullah bin Abu Malikah narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) does not see any problem in making up the Qada of Ramadan regularly."
"2324","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that according to him, there is no problem in performing the qada of Ramadan separately."
"2325","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas and Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) say that you can keep them separately and complete the number."
"2326","Sayyiduna Mu'azbin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about the qaza of Ramadan, so he said, \You count the count and fast as much as you want.\"""""
"2327","Sayyiduna Mu'azbin Jabal (RA) says, \You can make a difference in the Qadaa of Ramadan"," but count the count."""
"2328","Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) says, \You should keep count and do it whenever you want (i.e. do Qadaa)."""
"2329","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this about the Qadaa of Ramadan: If a person wants, he can keep it separately, and if he wants, he can keep it continuously."
"2330","The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Harah Ubaid bin Umayr in another chain of transmission."
"2331","/ 1 The same hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, with reference to Harah Ata of another chain of transmission."
"2332","Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas (RA) says that you can keep the Qadaa of Ramadan separately, because Allah has said this, then it will be counted in other days."
"2333","Muhammad bin Munkadar narrates that I have come to know that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about keeping the fasts of Ramadan separate. He said, \It is your will. What do you think?\"" Apart from Abu Bakr"," other narrators have narrated it as a received tradition"," however"," they have narrated it on the authority of Musa bin Uqbah"," on the authority of Abu Zubair on the authority of Sayyidna Jabir (RA) and this tradition is also not confirmed."""
"2334","Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about keeping the fasts of Ramadan separately. He said, \What do you think? If a person owes a debt and pays it in dirhams"," even if he pays it all in the same way"," will it be necessary for him to pay the debt or will he be considered as a blasphemer?\"" The people said yes! Ya Rasulullah! This hadith is narrated on the authority of Abu Zubair on the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"2335","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \If a person dies and there are some fasts on him"," then his wali fasts on his behalf is authentic\""."""
"2336","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Whoever dies and some fasts are due to him"," his guardian (heir) should fast on his behalf.\"""""
"2337","This tradition along with some other isnads has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA)."
"2338","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “My sister has passed away.” The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, “If she had a debt, would you have paid it?” He said yes! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \So Allah is more entitled to this (that his right be paid)."""
"2339","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words. This woman had submitted that she (the deceased) was required to fast for two consecutive months, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Allah's debt (has the right\"" to be paid)."""
"2340","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and said, 'My mother has passed away and she was required to fast for a month.' So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If your mother had a debt, would you have paid it on her behalf? He said yes! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The debt of Allah"," the Exalted"," is more entitled to be paid.\"""""
"2341","Yunus narrates Saeed bin Zayd (the narrator named Anbsa narrated this, he is the brother of Yunus) asked Nafi, who is the slave of Abdullah bin Umar, about a person who falls ill and his illness lasts for a long time. If he is unable to fast in the month of Ramadan, if he gives a piece of wheat to a poor person in exchange for each fast, then it will not be necessary for him to make up for it."
"2342","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that whoever is blessed with the time of Ramadan (and is able to fast for some reason) and is required to pay for a part of Ramadan (i.e. some of his fasts), then he should give a piece of wheat to a poor person for each fast."
"2343","Ata narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu said about a person who fell ill in Ramadan and later recovered, “He did not fast (in the first part) until he got the opportunity to fast in the last part. And when he is done with it, then he will fast the day that he neglected to do so."
"2344","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says about the person who neglects to make up Ramadan until he reaches the last part of Ramadan. He says that person will fast with the people and then he will also fast on the day he neglected and he will feed a poor person for each day."
"2345","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this about a person who cannot fast in the month of Ramadan due to illness, then he recovers and does not fast until the next Ramadan comes. He did not keep and in exchange for each day he will feed one resident."
"2346","Ata narrates that he heard Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) saying: He says about a person who falls ill in the month of Ramadan and does not fast, then he recovers, or a person who fasts until he is blessed with the next Ramadan. Will feed. His tradition is authentic."
"2347","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) says that whoever neglects the fasts of Ramadan until the next Ramadan comes, then that person will fast that Ramadan."
"2348","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a person is not healthy in the middle of Ramadan, he will fast the current Ramadan (i.e. fasts to make up for it) and eat food from the previous Ramadan, and it will not be necessary for him to make up (for the fasts of the previous Ramadan), but whoever is healthy and does not fast until the next Ramadan comes, he will fast the current Ramadan. will feed him and when his fasts of this month are over, then he will make up for the fasts of the previous Ramadan."
"2349","Ziyad bin Jabir narrates, I remember a person came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) and asked him a question, and that person said: He had vowed that he would fast every Wednesday. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said, \Allah has ordered the fulfillment of the vow and the Prophet (PBUH) has forbidden us to fast on the day of sacrifice. This is an authentic document.\"""""
"2350","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we have kept twenty-nine fasts more than the number of thirty times we kept with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (i.e., in his holy time) (ie, the month of Ramadan is sometimes twenty-nine days long)."
"2351","This is narrated about Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her: She was asked, O Mother of the Believers! Can the month of Ramadan be twenty-nine days? He replied, \I have fasted twenty-nine times more than I have fasted thirty times with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (i.e. in his time of the Holy Prophet)\"". Its chain of transmission is authentic and the tradition before it is not proven"," because its narrator is Abd al-Ala bin Abul Mus and is obsolete."""
"2352","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that we have fasted thirty times with the Holy Prophet (SAW) more than twenty-nine fasts."
"2353","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) Sayyidna Umar (RA) made a vow during the Jahiliyyah era that he would perform one-night Itikaaf in Masjid Haram."
"2354","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, made a vow during the time of Jahiliyya that he would perform one night of I’tikaf in Masjid al-Haram."
"2355","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Fasting is not obligatory on a person who performs I'tikaaf. However"," if he makes it obligatory on himself (also to fast)"," the ruling (will be different). The Sheikh has narrated this hadith as a valid hadith"," while other narrators have not transmitted it as a valid hadith."""
"2356","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \I'tikaaf is valid only with fasting.\"" Swedish narrators are unique in quoting this."""
"2357","Sayyiduna Huzaifah (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying, \Every mosque in which there is a muezzin and an imam can perform I'tikaf.\"" The narrator of this tradition"," Zahaq"," has not heard the hadiths from Sayyidna Huzaifah."""
"2358","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a person who performs itikaaf can attend the Friday prayer, attend a funeral and visit the sick."
"2359","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A person who does itikaaf can visit the sick, attend a funeral, go for Friday, go to his home (but cannot stay with them for long)."
"2360","Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Umar (RA) narrates this about Sayyiduna Umar (RA) He asked the Prophet (PBUH) about I'tikaf, it was obligatory for a young man, so the Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to perform I'tikaf and also fast."
"2361","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) has narrated this saying, 'Sayyidna Umar (RA) said to the Prophet (PBUH) that I had made a vow that I would perform I'tikaf for one day,' then the Prophet (PBUH) said, 'You should perform I'tikaf and fast as well.' I have heard Shaykh Abu Bakr Nishapuri saying, “He says that this hadeeth has been rejected because the authentic disciples of Amro bin Dinar did not narrate it, including Ibn Jarij, Ibn Uyaynah, Hamad bin Salamah, Hamad bin Zayd and others, while its narrator Ibn Badil is weak.”"
"2362","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates; The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform I'tikaf in the last ten days of the month of Ramadan."
"2363","Urwa bin Zubair and Saeed bin Musaib narrated this. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) told them that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform I’tikaaf in the last ten days of the month of Ramadan until Allah passed away. He will not participate in the funeral, he will not go to visit the sick, he will not touch a woman and he will not have intercourse with her, and I'tikaf can only be in the mosque where congregational prayers are held, and the person who performs I'tikaf will be ordered to fast. Narrator) is the word of Zuhri, who has recorded it in the hadith, due to which this illusion has occurred, Allah knows best, but the narrator Hisham bin Sulaiman has not mentioned it"
"2364","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform I’tikaaf in the last ten days of Ramadan until Allah passed away. I'tikaaf will only be in the place where congregational prayers are offered, and the Sunnah for the person performing I'tikaf is to fast."
"2365","Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, Sayyidna Umar, may God be pleased with him, had vowed during the time of polytheism that he would do itikaf and fast. After he accepted Islam, he reported to the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about this. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \You fulfill your vow"," its chain of transmission is good.\"" The narrator named Saeed bin Basheer is unique in quoting it in these words."""
"2366","Abu Ishaq Khwarazmi narrates: I asked Asim Ahol, can a fasting person perform maswak? He answered yes! I discovered that both wet and dry maswak can be used. He answered yes! I have a question, can I do both in the beginning, the end or the end of the day? He answered yes! I inquired from whom is this said? So he replied that it was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the narrator of this tradition, Abu Ishaq Khwarazmi, is weak."
"2367","Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi narrates this on the authority of his father: I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rubbing his mouth while fasting. Other narrators are more authentic than Asim bin Ubaidullah."
"2368","Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi narrates on the authority of his parents: I have seen the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing maswak while fasting."
"2369","This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads."
"2370","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that you are allowed to brush your teeth until Asr prayer, when you pray Asr, then put it aside."
"2371","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \The best thing for a fasting person is to brush his teeth.\"" In one hadith"," these words are \""One of the best things for a fasting person to do is to brush his teeth.\"""""
"2372","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when you fast, brush your teeth in the morning and don't brush your teeth in the evening. The reason for this is that the lips of a fasting person will be dry in the evening."
"2373","This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Khabab (RA) along with another chain of transmission. A narrator named Abu Umar Kaisan is not authentic and there are no narrators known between him and Sayyiduna Ali."
"2374","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when an old person is unable to fast, then he should take one medicine for each fast."
"2375","Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr (RA) narrates that in the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), we broke the fast one day in the month of Ramadan when it was overcast, but later the sun came out (it turned out that it was not time to break the fast). So he replied that it was necessary to do so. Its certificate is valid and proven."
"2376","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2377","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) has said this about the saying of Allah, \And for those who do not have the power"," their ransom is to feed a poor person. He means a poor person. Allah says"," \""Let the one who does good be generous. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that if he feeds another poor person"," if it remains too much"," he says that this order is not abrogated"," but this leave has been given to the old man who cannot afford to fast"," and this order to feed is for the person who knows that he will no longer have the strength to fast."""
"2378","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that (God is the guide) the redemption of those who have the power is to feed a poor person. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) says that those who do not have the power to do so, they are bound to feed one poor person, and whoever wants to do good in the afterlife, should feed one more poor person. So it is better if in this case the leave is given only to the old man who does not have the strength to fast and it is given to the sick person who knows that he will never be cured again, his certificate is correct."
"2379","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says (may Allah guide him) that the ransom for those who do not have the strength to do so is to feed a poor person (may Allah guide him) “Whoever should do good after his death” means that he should feed one more poor person (may Allah guide him) “then it will be better for him. There is more for you. (Sayyidna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that this leave is given only to the old man who does not have the strength to fast, and to the sick person who knows that he will not be cured."
"2380","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that this leave is for the old man, he should stop fasting and feed a poor person for one day, and no qaza will be required for him. His certificate is correct."
"2381","Ata narrates that he heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) reciting this: \And those who do not have the strength to do so"," their ransom is to feed the poor.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says that this order is not abrogated. It means an old man or a woman. The answer is that they will never be able to fast. So they should feed one poor person for each day. This tradition is correct."""
"2382","Saeed bin Jabirbayan says that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said to his mother, who was pregnant and was nursing a child, (she said:) You are among those people who do not have the strength to fast."
"2383","Saeed bin Jubayr narrates this about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said that a tuberculosis patient who is disappointed that he will be cured and will never be able to fast, such a person will not fast and will feed one poor person for every day."
"2384","Saeed bin Jubeer narrated this about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. He had a maidservant who was nursing a child. She fell ill, so Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, instructed her that you should not fast, and give food (as fidya) and keep qazana. This hadith is authentic."
"2385","Saeed bin Jubayr narrates that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) or perhaps Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) has said that a pregnant woman who breastfeeds will not fast, and she will not make up for it later (rather, she will feed the poor). This tradition and the following tradition are authentic."
"2386","According to Mujahidbayan, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, recited this verse: \For those who do not have the strength"," it is obligatory to feed a poor person as a ransom.\"" Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with him"," says that this means an old man who cannot afford to fast."""
"2387","Ikramah narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) used to recite this verse, \And those who do not have the power to do it"," it is obligatory on them.\"" Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) used to say that this verse was abrogated."""
"2388","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that his wife asked him, \She was pregnant.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said"," \""You should stop fasting and feed a poor person for one day.\"""""
"2389","Narrated by Nafi, a daughter of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with her, she was the wife of a Qureshi, when she became pregnant, she felt very thirsty, so Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with her, instructed her to stop fasting and feed a poor person for one day."
"2390","Ayyub narrates that one year Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) could not fast due to his weakness."
"2391","Qatadah narrates that Sayyiduna Anas (may God be pleased with him) became weak before his death, so he did not fast, he instructed his wife to feed one poor person for every day."
"2392","Mujahid narrates: I heard Qays ibn Sa'ib narrating that the ransom of the month of Ramadan will be given by a man who feeds one poor person for every day, so feed two poor people on my behalf."
"2393","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says, \If a person becomes old and is unable to fast"," then it is obligatory on him to pay a full amount of wheat for each day.\"""""
"2394","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: “If a person owes a debt, if it is paid by him, then it is paid by him.” The Prophet (PBUH) said similar things about Hajj and fasting."
"2395","Muhammad bin Hasan, regarding his father (Hasan), his father (Imam Zain al-Abidin, may God bless him and grant him peace), his grandfather (Imam Hussain, may God bless him and grant him peace), narrates this statement of Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib, may God bless him and grant him peace, a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said, O Messenger of God! I have become a victim of death. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked what has caused you to become a victim of death. He said, \I have had intercourse with his wife during Ramadan.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired"," \""Do you have any slaves or concubines?\"" He did not answer this request! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed that he should be given fifteen sa’s. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," “You feed these sixty poor people.” He said"," “By the One who has sent you with the truth! Has been paid."""
"2396","Amir bin Saad narrates the statement of his father (Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2397","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates, A person broke his fast in the month of Ramadan, and the Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to free a slave as an atonement, or to fast for two months, or to feed sixty poor people. Give charity, he said, O Messenger of Allah, I do not know of anyone who needs it more than me, then the Prophet smiled until his side teeth were visible, then he said, \Eat it.\"" Some narrators have narrated in this tradition that this person had broken the fast of Ramadan and he was given the option to make expiation (to choose one of the above three cases)"," but most of the narrators have narrated that this person had broken his fast by having intercourse"," and the Prophet (peace be upon him) first ordered him to expiate by freeing a slave. When he could not afford it"," he ordered him to feed sixty poor people."""
"2398","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have perished (perhaps these are the words) I have perished (myself). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast for two consecutive months. Feed it to your family."
"2399","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) gave this instruction to a person who breaks the fast in Ramadan (after that the narrator has mentioned it according to the previous hadith), but these words are superfluous in the names, you should eat it and fast for one day."
"2400","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “I have had intercourse with my wife during Ramadan (fasting). I can't even do that. The narrator narrates, a basket of fifteen Sa'a dates was brought to the Prophet, and he said, \Take it and feed it yourself.\"" He said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," we need it the most in the whole city.\"" These words are from a narrator named Bakr and narrated by a narrator named Muhammad bin Abu Hafsa."""
"2401","The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: A sack was brought and there was a measure in which there were fifteen sa's, 'It is also', there were fifteen sa's of dates."
"2402","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was told that he had intercourse with his wife during Ramadan (while fasting). I do not have that. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast for two consecutive months. He said: I cannot afford it. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Feed sixty poor people. He said, \Are you more needy than yourself and your family?\"" He said"," \""I have no one more needy than myself and my family.\"""""
"2403","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: “Whoever does not fast one month of Ramadan, he will be required to fast for a month, his chain of transmission is not proven."
"2404","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever does not fast one day of Ramadan without any illness or leave, even fasting forever will not be a reward for him."
"2405","Rabi'ah bin Abdul Rahman says that whoever does not fast one day of Ramadan, he will fast for twelve days. This is because Allah has preferred fasting one month to twelve months."
"2406","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) has said that if a person does not fast in Ramadan without leave or illness, even fasting all the time will not make up for him."
"2407","Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Hudhafa Sahmi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on my camel in the days of Mina to announce, O people, these are the days of eating, drinking and companionship. The narrator of this tradition is weak."
"2408","Sayyidna Hamza Aslami narrates: He saw a man who was going to the residences of the people during the days of Tashriq in Mina, he was riding a camel and he was saying: Be careful not to fast during these days because these are the days of eating and drinking and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is among you. Not done."
"2409","Qatadah narrates the statement of Anas, the Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade fasting on five days of the year, the day of Eid al-Fitr, the day of Eid al-Adha and the three days of the days of Tashreeq. A narrator named Uthman narrates, We have narrated the same hadith regarding Muhammad bin Khalid."
"2410","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed Sayyidna Umar bin Hazm (may Allah be pleased with him) about Sadaqah al-Fitr, that it should be half a saa of wheat or one saa of dates."
"2411","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when there is milk in the udder, do it with milk, and when there is no wool (on the animal's back), then do it with milk."
"2412","Masoud bin Haqm Zarqi' narrates this with reference to one of the companions of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Hudhafa, may God be pleased with him, announced this during the days of Tashreeq, under the command of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace! These are the days of Eid, these are the days of eating, drinking and remembering, so only a person who is a pilgrim or a pilgrim who does not have a sacrificial animal with him, or who has not fasted continuously during the days of Hajj should fast on these days."
"2413","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates when this verse was revealed, \And it is obligatory upon the people to perform Hajj to the House of Allah for the sake of Allah"," and it is obligatory upon the person who has the power to reach it.\"" So a person stood up"," he said"," O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by \""sibyl\"" here? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ``Zad travel and ride.''"""
"2414","Amro bin Shoaib quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, in reference to his father, \In reference to his grandfather"," \""The way to reach the house of Allah is the journey of Adsafar Adar."""
"2415","Amro bin Shoaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father. A person said, O Messenger of Allah! What makes Hajj obligatory? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zadrah and ride (to be available)."
"2416","Amro bin Shoaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father. A person said, O Messenger of Allah! What does sable mean? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Zad Safar and Sawari\""."""
"2417","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) (Allah the Exalted said) \It is obligatory upon people to perform Hajj to the House of Allah"," whoever has the means to reach it.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I said"," O Messenger of Allah! What does sable mean? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Zad Safar and Sawari\""."""
"2418","This same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Anas, along with another chain of transmission."
"2419","This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2420","This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa."
"2421","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (SAW) was asked about the saying of Allah, “And the Hajj to the House of Allah for the sake of Allah is obligatory on those who have a way to reach it.” The sages have discovered who is more virtuous? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \In which the Talbiyyah is recited aloud"," the blood of the sacrificial animal has been shed.\"""""
"2422","This same tradition and chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the route to Hajj."
"2423","Muhammad bin Ubad narrates that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him, came to us and told us that a person said, O Messenger of God! What is meant by Hajj? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zaad Safar and Sawari (to be available)."
"2424","The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with another chain of transmission with reference to Sayyidna Hasan al-Basri. \And for the sake of Allah"," it is obligatory upon the people to perform Hajj to the House of Allah"," whoever has the means to reach it.\"" The people said"," O Messenger of Allah! What does sable mean? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zaad Safar and Sawari (to be available)."""
"2425","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: It was asked, O Messenger of Allah! Is performing Hajj every year (obligatory?) The Prophet (PBUH) said no! Rather, a Hajj (obligatory) is offered, what is meant by the way up to it? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zaad Safar and Sawari (to be available)."
"2426","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: It was asked, O Messenger of Allah! Means how to reach it? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zaad Safar and Sawari (to be available)."
"2427","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) has quoted the saying of Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab (RA) 'Sabil means to be able to travel and ride."
"2428","Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, narrates from the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, that, “By Allah, the Hajj of the House is the right of Allah upon the people, that whoever is able to reach his house, should perform the Hajj.” He was asked about this verse. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \It means that you have the back of the ride.\"""""
"2429","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Sayyida Zubayah (may Allah be pleased with her) who was ill. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then make up your mind for Hajj and make a condition with it and say: O Allah! Where I am not able to go further"," I will give Ihram Kol."""
"2430","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) visited Sayyida Zaba’ah bint Zubair (RA) and he said, “O Messenger of Allah! I intend to perform Hajj, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them, when putting on Ihram, make a condition that where I am not able to go further, I will open Ihram, then you will have the right to do so."
"2431","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyid al-Zabaa'ah that you intend to perform Hajj and make a condition that I will open Ihram where I am no longer able to go further."
"2432","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) took a bath, then he put on his clothes, then when he came to Dhul-Halifa, he offered two rak'ahs there, then he sat on his camel, when his ride stopped, from there he put on the Ihram for Hajj (i.e., he intended to do it)."
"2433","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that this is a Sunnah: When a person begins to put on Ihram, he should perform ghusl when he begins to enter Makkah (he should also perform ghusl at that time)."
"2434","Al-Khahir ibn Zayd narrated this on the authority of his father (Zayd ibn Thabit, may God be pleased with him) that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took a ghusl before putting on Ihram. Ibn Sa’id states that this hadith is weak."
"2435","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2436","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) took a ghusl at the place of \Fasq\"" before entering Makkah."""
"2437","Abu Ubaidah bin Hudhaifa narrates that a gentleman has narrated this. I used to ask people about the hadith of Sayyidna Udi bin Hatim (RA) 'He was by my side', but I did not ask him if I then came to him. When I came to serve him, he said to me, ``Adi bin Hatim! Accept Islam and you will be safe. After that, he mentioned the entire hadith, which contains these words: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said to me, “Soon a woman will depart from “Hira” (a place called) and she will circumambulate the House of Allah without being sheltered by anyone."
"2438","Sayyidna Adi bin Hatim (RA) came and stayed with the Holy Prophet (SAW) and the Prophet (SAW) said to him, “Soon a time will come when a woman will leave Hira (a place called) without seeking the shelter of a person until she performs Hajj to the House of Allah, and a time will soon come when the wealth will be so much that a man will wish to find someone to receive this charity. Anhu narrates: I saw a woman who left without seeking shelter from anyone, until she performed Hajj to the House of Allah. This tradition is short."
"2439","Muhammad bin Huzaifah narrates that we used to recite the hadith of Sayyiduna Udi bin Hatim (RA) to each other. He used to live in a village on the outskirts of Kufa. I thought that it would be appropriate if I went to him and heard this hadith from him. So I attended his service. ``Adi said, \When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent"," I escaped and went to a distant part of the Islamic kingdom. Then I thought that I should be present in his service. If he is truthful"," I will accept his word. When I (in his service) the Ayatullah stood for me. The narrator narrates (after that he narrated to me the entire hadith in which this statement is made) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me"," “Have you gone to Hira? I did not submit! But I know its place. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""The time will soon come when a woman will leave there without taking shelter from anyone.\"" Sayyiduna Adi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Then I saw a woman who set out from Hira and circumambulated the House of Kaaba (arrived at Makkah). This tradition is short."""
"2440","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person came to Madinah, 'The Prophet (PBUH) opened the gate, where are you staying? He said to such and such a woman, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Has he closed the door of your children? A woman should perform Hajj only when there is a dear Muharram with her.\"""""
"2441","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrated this saying about the Prophet (PBUH): “The Prophet (PBUH) did not allow a woman to perform Hajj whose husband was present, even though she had wealth."
"2442","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) saying, \No woman should travel for three days or go for Hajj unless her husband is with her.\"""""
"2443","Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The day of 'Arafah is the day in which people recognize each other.\"""""
"2444","Ya'qub bin Zayd quoted the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father: \Arafah is the day in which people recognize each other.\"""""
"2445","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that your Eid-ul-Fitr day is when you celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr and the day of Eid-ul-Adha is when you celebrate Eid-ul-Adha."
"2446","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \The day of your Eid-ul-Fitr is when you celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr"," and the day of Eid-ul-Adha is when you celebrate Eid-ul-Adha.\"""""
"2447","Muhammad bin Mankader has quoted on the authority of Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that a narrator named Abu Hisham narrates this."
"2448","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the words \I am here\"" were included in the Talbiyah of the Holy Prophet (SAW)."""
"2449","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I took the words of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastily while he was reciting them. \O Allah! I am present! O Allah! I am present! I am present! You have no partner"," I am present! Verily"," all praise and praise is reserved for You"," and the kingdom also has no partner.\"""""
"2450","This same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, in which these words of his are mentioned. The talbiya of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was, 'After that, he has narrated as per the previous hadith' in which these words have been quoted additionally. The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) was repeating these words."
"2451","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to put on Ihram, he used to wash his holy head with khatmi and ashnan and apply olive oil on it. This happened many times."
"2452","Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the months of Hajj are Shawwal, Dhul-Qa'dah and the first ten days of Dhul-Hijj."
